  "content": "<p><strong>Instructor:</strong> Dennis Freeman</p>\n<p><strong>Description:</strong> Sampling produces a discrete-time (digital) signal from a continuous-time (physical) phenomenon. Anti-aliasing and reconstruction filters remove unnecessary frequencies while retaining enough information to reconstruct the original signal.</p>\n",
